.TH CODEX-USAGE-TRAY 1 "July 2026" "codex-usage-tray 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codex-usage-tray \- display OpenAI Codex usage limits in the Ubuntu system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codex-usage-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codex-usage-tray
starts an unofficial GTK 3 AppIndicator application that reads usage limits
from the local OpenAI Codex app-server and displays the remaining allowance
in the Ubuntu GNOME top panel.
.PP
OpenAI Codex must be installed and authenticated separately.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/codex-usage-tray.desktop
System-wide autostart entry used to launch the application after login.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3, GTK 3, PyGObject, Ayatana AppIndicator, and an authenticated
OpenAI Codex installation.
